# Implement gate (hard rule)

**Do not edit KiCad projects, schematic/PCB sources, or fabrication exports** unless the operator **explicitly** commands implementation in that turn or a prior turn they have not revoked.

## Commands that authorize design work

Only these (or clear equivalents in the same message):

- `implement`
- `ship`
- `patch`
- `fix` / `bugfix` when clearly directed at the board design

## Does NOT authorize design edits

- `triage`, `kickoff`, analysis, Q&A, "no code", "no design"
- Locked spec, kickoff answers, "this is fine"
- Pipeline / phase markdown updates during triage or kickoff (those flows have their own rules)

## Pipeline docs

- **triage** / **kickoff**: may edit `docs/todo/*` only — no KiCad project edits.
- **implement** / **ship** / **patch**: KiCad + fab outputs allowed; pipeline close-out when ship/DoD says so.
- Phase close-out: move Done `docs/todo/phase*.md` → `docs/todo/_archive/` — [`.cursor/rules/phase-archive.mdc`](phase-archive.mdc).

## When unsure

Stop and ask: **triage**, **kickoff**, or **implement**? Do not start schematic or layout work without a kickoff lock on **R1** (architecture) or the relevant phase.

## Conflicts

User Rule **Collaboration standards** wins. This rule makes the implement gate explicit for wanos-pcb.
